## **2\. B2B Value Proposition Translation (Stakeholder Model)**

Core premise: Good B2B messaging is translation. Different roles speak different languages and care about different things — different workflows (use cases), different goals (outcomes). One universal value prop resonates with no one.

### **The Five Stakeholder Types**

| Stakeholder | Role Example | Message Focus | Outcome Type |
| ----- | ----- | ----- | ----- |
| Champion | InfoSec Director | Use case \+ capability \+ product outcome | Product outcome |
| User Influencer | Sales Teams | Use case \+ capability \+ product outcome | Product outcome |
| Operations Influencer | Head of Sales | Business outcome (no use case needed) | Business outcome |
| Decision Maker | CEO | Business outcome | Business outcome |
| Financial Influencer | CFO | Quantified business outcome | Hard numbers |

### **The Translation Chain**

Product capability → Product outcome (Champion \+ User) → Business outcome (Ops \+ Decision Maker) → Quantified business outcome (Financial Influencer)

Vanta example (security questionnaire product):

* Capability: AI structures security answers and fills questionnaires automatically  
* Product outcome (Champion/InfoSec): Spend less time answering questionnaires  
* Product outcome (User/Sales): Get accurate security responses without having to bother InfoSec  
* Business outcome (Head of Sales): Move through security reviews faster — sales velocity  
* Business outcome (CEO): Close more deals faster  
* Quantified outcome (CFO): Closing 1 extra deal per quarter \= extra $500K ARR

### **Who Owns What**

Marketing focuses on Champion and User Influencer — earn trust at the product outcome level, with the person who actually uses it.

Sales focuses on Operations Influencer, Decision Maker, and Financial Influencer — translate product value into business value, with the people who approve it.

### **The Failure Mode**

A "universal value proposition" that tries to speak to everyone speaks to no one. If you haven't done the translation work per stakeholder, your message lands with zero of them — not all of them.

